# Never ignore anything under .github, regardless of any blanket pattern
# above (e.g. *.yaml/*.json): those already-tracked workflow files aren't
# actually hidden from plain git commands (git only applies .gitignore to
# untracked paths), but tools with their own gitignore-pattern-matching
# file-discovery (e.g. pre-commit's own file list for hooks like prettier)
# don't make that same tracked/untracked distinction, and were silently
# dropping every .github/workflows/*.yaml file as a result.
!.github/**
!/renovate.json
